  "verdict": "Underpowered: pose covers 2 matches and each interval resamples those matches. Of 1347 labeled receptions, the nearest defender was square/in front in 1100 (82%), side-on in 240 (18%), and back-to in 7 (1%). Side-on minus square/in front: xshot_player_possession_max: effect 0.0367 (interval 0.0288 to 0.0451, n_side=146, n_square=848, supported=true); receiver_xthreat: effect 0.0033 (interval 0.0023 to 0.0041, n_side=228, n_square=1054, supported=true); possession_epv_total: effect 0.0014 (interval 0.0005 to 0.0026, n_side=237, n_square=1091, supported=true); pass_epv_total: effect 0.0017 (interval 0.0010 to 0.0026, n_side=206, n_square=955, supported=true). Back-to has n=7, below 20, so those intervals are not used for support. supported=true because the side-on minus square/in front interval excludes zero for: xshot_player_possession_max, receiver_xthreat, possession_epv_total, pass_epv_total. Unlabeled receptions: goalkeeper_receiver=78, labeled=1347, no_pose=14, undefined_vector=3, unreliable_shoulders=13.",
  "notes": "Two matches only, so every interval is underpowered and this is not a practical metric. A narrow interval means the two matches agree, not that the league-wide effect is precise. Back-to has too few events to support a contrast. Outcomes are xshot_player_possession_max, player_targeted_xthreat on the received pass, possession_epv_total, and pass_epv_total."
}
